#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
dtRadar — Vintage NWS NEXRAD Doppler Radar, GOES Satellite & HF Solar Space-Weather Console for CDE

Features:
  - Authentic 1980s/1990s CDE / OSF-Motif 3D beveled meteorological & propagation workstation:
      * CDE `xrdb` palette integration, glowing cyan-green Vacuum Fluorescent Displays (VFD),
        warm incandescent analog dial backlighting, and sunken #FFF7E9 / Amber teletype strip.
      * Pre-configured Home QTH: W1AW / FN31pr (41.7292° N, -72.7083° W, Newington, CT),
        nearest NEXRAD station KBOX, nearest METAR KBDL, GOES-16 `ne` Northeast sector,
        all user-configurable in the top bar and persisted in `~/.config/dtradar/config.json`.
  - 4 Switchable Tactical CRT Views + Animated [▶ LOOP] / Frame Scrubber + PPI Sweep Arm:
      1. NEXRAD DOPPLER MAP: Zoomable/pannable dark tactical map (OSM dark-LUT base tiles +
         embedded vector world & US state outlines) overlaid with live 6-frame (30-min) Iowa
         Environmental Mesonet NEXRAD Base Reflectivity (`N0Q`) tiles, standard dBZ color scale,
         50/100/150/200 km range rings, optional rotating green phosphor PPI sweep arm, and
         active NWS CAP warning polygons (`api.weather.gov/alerts/active`).
      2. NWS STATION RIDGE RADAR: Direct NOAA RIDGE station still & multi-frame `_loop.gif`
         viewer (`KBOX`, `KOKX`, `KLWX`, `KCBX`, `KMTX`, `CONUS`, or custom site)
         with PIL multi-frame GIF unpacker, zoom/pan, and frame scrubber.
      3. GOES-18 / 16 SATELLITE: Live NOAA NESDIS STAR imagery (`Northern Rockies GeoColor`,
         `Band-13 Clean IR`, `Water Vapor Band-09`, `CONUS GeoColor`, `Full Disk Earth`) plus
         SWPC `Aurora Oval North`, zoomable & pannable.
      4. HF SOLAR & PROPAGATION DESK: Live NOAA SWPC 6-hour GOES X-Ray Flare Flux logarithmic
         chart (`A/B/C/M/X`), Planetary `Kp` 3-hour bar graph, `10.7cm SFI` / Sunspot / Solar
         Wind telemetry, and calculated HF Amateur Band Condition Matrix (`80m–6m` Day & Night
         `GOOD / FAIR / POOR` + VHF Aurora/E-Skip indicators).
  - Right Instrument Rack + Bottom METAR/TAF Teletype:
      * 3 Backlit Analog Needle Dials: BAROMETER (28.5..31.0 inHg, STORM/CHANGE/FAIR),
        WIND COMPASS & KT/MPH (360° compass rose + gust VFD), TEMP / DEWPOINT / RH% (-20..110°F).
      * Sunken `#FFF7E9` / Amber Teletype Strip with live raw + decoded METAR/TAF & NWS Alerts.
"""

